= The <span style="color: #0dba1e;">Green Front</span>

In an effort to act as a counterweight to the growing strength of the Rural People's Movement, the bulk of organised agrculture has formed an umbrella organisation called the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">**Green Front**</span>, affording agricultural interests in the <span style="color: #000000;">**Center Party**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> more influence in their respective parties.
Built on the negotiations back in March, the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">**Green Front**</span> aims to draft a comprehensive farm program to address the structural deficiencies in German Agriculture. [? if agriculture_minister_party = 'Z': As we currently hold the Agriculture Ministry, the onus will fall on us to implement the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">**Green Front**</span>'s economic program in the coming months. ?] This increased focus on agricultural issues might alienate our substantial worker base while this extensive cooperation with anti-republican parties has led to outcry from the left of the party.

With members from the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #909090;">**DBP**</span>, this disparate coalition of Estate Agriculture and smallholder farmers is testament to the increasingly concering situation in the countryside. However, not all is well, as the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span> have managed to use the leadership elections of the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">Green Front</span> as a proxy in their bid for control of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span>.  


- @results: The delegates vote...

@results
go-to: schiele if (schiele_points > 3); hepp if (schiele_points <= 3)

- @schiele
- @hepp

@schiele
title: A triumph for the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>
on-arrival: rural_z += 1; rural_dnvp += 4; rural_other += 4; rural_nsdap -= 3; right_strength += 5; right_dissent -= 5; dnvp_relations += 5; left_dissent += 6; green_front_leader = "Schiele"

As expected, Martin Schiele, with strong backing from most of the <span style="color: #385A38;">**RLB**</span> and <span style="color: #000000;">**VdB**</span>'s delegates, has clinched the Presidency of the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">Green Front</span>. As a widely respected figure in the agrarian community, his election has cemented the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>’s continued domination of the agrarian lobby. While his close ties to President Hindenburg might prove to be beneficial, some in the <span style="color: #000000;">**VdB**</span> worry that it might impede his efforts at drafting a workable farm program. 

@hepp
title: The dark horse rises
on-arrival: rural_z += 1; rural_dnvp -= 2; rural_cnblp += 5; rural_nsdap -= 1; right_strength += 3; right_dissent -= 3; dnvp_relations += 3; left_dissent += 4; special_interests += 10; green_front_leader = "Hepp"; dvp_right += 1; ddp_right += 1

In light of a growing disillusionment with the conservative agrarian establishment represented by Schiele of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, the delegates have instead turned to Karl Hepp of the fledgling <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> to lead the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">Green Front</span>. A rebuff to the widely respected Schiele, this has prompted outrage from delegates of the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>.

Situated on the right wing of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span>, Hepp’s election signifies the growing influence of middle class smallholders in agrarian organisations as opposed to the traditionally dominant Junkers. Unwilling to prop up the insolvent Junker estates, it is widely expected that he will abandon plans for the creation of an Eastern Aid Fund and orient the <span style="color: #0dba1e;">Green Front</span> towards the interests of smallholder farmers in Northern and Southern Germany. Overall, his election has bolstered the legitimacy of the <span style="color: #006400;">**CNBLP**</span> as an alternative to the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>, as well as weakening the agrarian elements in the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**DNVP**</span>. [? if dnvp_leader == 'Hugenberg' : Against the backdrop of Hugenberg’s attempts to consolidate power, this is a severe setback for Schiele and might force him to reconsider his ‘wait and see’ approach. ?]
